Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Factorial Causal Scenario Attribution for Species Distribution Models
Version: 0.23.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Factorial causal scenario attribution for species distribution
    models. A 2 x 2 design (current, climate-only, land-use-only, joint)
    estimates climate main effects, land-use main effects, the joint change and
    their interaction on a fitted suitability surface, with continuous and
    binary range summaries, support diagnostics and model disagreement.
    Paired driver-only and retained-driver comparisons remain available for
    within-scenario explanation. Random forest, MaxEnt and generalized additive
    model engines support a data-driven elastic-net screen, spatial
    cross-validation, ensemble prediction and projection.
    The factorial contrasts are model-based causal scenario attributions under
    explicit assumptions; they are not identified real-world causal effects,
    occurrence probabilities or realised distributions.
